0027: generation_strategy:
0028:   approach: output-first
0029:   steps:
0030:     - Decide reached or stuck (~50/50), then pick N (1-4 for reached; 2-4 for stuck)
0031:     - Pick grid size H=W (10-20, H/N >= 5)
0032:     - Carve channel: divide grid into coarse cells (spacing N+2), self-avoiding random walk
0033:       on coarse grid, render as N-wide corridors connecting consecutive cell centers
0034:     - Place dest at one end of the path (touching grid edge), mover at the other end (near grid edge, interior)
0035:     - For stuck: narrow 1-3 segments between mover and dest to width < N;
0036:       verify with BFS on NxN-placement grid that dest is unreachable
0037:     - Build output: place mover at BFS-farthest reachable position from mover start; fill start with river;
0038:       place dest only if stuck (if reached, mover overwrites dest)
0039:     - Derive input: restore mover to start, restore dest, fill mover's output position with river
0040:     - Final validation: main(input) == expected output
